//
// Expected: c0 at one session and at two.
//
// The dealer leaks k after splitting it two-of-three. Each sharing draws its
// own polynomial, so k is one point of it and fixes no share by itself: s1 is
// as secret as before. A share was once treated as an ordinary function of k,
// and the attacker "constructed" every share from the secret alone.
// threshold_secret_and_share_reveal_third.vp is the counterweight.
attacker[passive]
principal Dealer[
	generates k
	s1, s2, s3 = THRESHOLD_SPLIT[2](k)
	leaks k
]
Dealer -> Bob: [k]
principal Bob[
	_ = HASH(k)
]
queries[
	confidentiality? s1
]
